.TH SJMIN 1 "November 2026" "simdjson" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sjmin \- remove insignificant white space from a JSON document
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sjmin
[\fB\-o\fR \fIout_file\fR] [\fIfile\fR]
.br
.B sjmin
\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-v\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sjmin
minifies a JSON document with the SIMD routines of the simdjson library:
it removes the spaces, tabs, line feeds and carriage returns that appear
outside of strings, and copies everything else unchanged.
Strings, numbers and the order of keys are left as they are.
.PP
.B sjmin
reads \fIfile\fR, or standard input when \fIfile\fR is absent or is
\fB\-\fR, and writes the result to standard output. No line feed is
added after the document.
.PP
The input is not parsed and not validated: invalid JSON produces
invalid output, and the UTF-8 encoding is not checked. The only
error detected in the content is a string that is not terminated
before the end of the input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fIout_file\fR
write the result to \fIout_file\fR instead of standard output;
\fIout_file\fR may be the input file, which is read completely first
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display a short help and exit
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.TP
.B \-\-
treat the remaining argument as a file name, even if it starts with \fB\-\fR
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
success
.TP
.B 1
the input could not be read, contains an unterminated string, or the
output could not be written
.TP
.B 2
invalid command line
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Minify a file to standard output:
.B sjmin data.json
.TP
Minify standard input into a file:
.B curl \-s https://example.com/data.json | sjmin \-o data.min.json
.TP
Minify a file in place:
.B sjmin \-o data.json data.json
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jq (1)
.PP
https://github.com/simdjson/simdjson
.SH AUTHOR
Written by the simdjson development team.
